  "created": "2026-10-23T12:28:22.117Z",
  "description": "An embeddable holographic SQL database for .NET: transactional (ACID with a write-ahead log), columnar storage with compiled predicates, holo-native constant-time integer aggregates, and hash joins, an optional Pleroma aggregate plane (exact, derived summaries of small-domain columns that answer WHERE aggregates, multi-column GROUP BY, COUNT(DISTINCT), MIN/MAX and equi-join COUNT/SUM, declining to the engine outside its caps), a Pleroma page store (exact Phasor Pleroma and sparse pages as durable, larger-than-memory data with concurrent readers, a crash-safe add journal, restore points, an event journal, check-prime verification and parity repair), with an optional durable larger-than-memory tier (paged buffer-pool + write-ahead log, cold pages demand-paged from disk, a CRC-32C on every data page, UPDATE and DELETE by key or index, and statements larger than the buffer pool). INT / TEXT / REAL columns, INT or TEXT/GUID primary keys, SQL NULL on columns declared NULL (three-valued logic, IS [NOT] NULL, aggregates that skip NULLs), and schema evolution via CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS / ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN. An EvalApp-backed data-parallel query path (parallel scans, group-by, top-K, and SIMD real aggregates). Built for real-time metrics: live aggregate reads (whole-table and grouped counts/sums) are served lock-free from a snapshot published after each write, so a streaming ingest never stalls a dashboard read; ApplyChanges and INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE apply a change feed of upserts and deletes as one atomic batch (readers see all of it or none, one log commit), across several tables in one call when a source transaction touches more than one, and KeyDigest fingerprints an INT key set in one pass; summary tables (CREATE SUMMARY TABLE) keep no rows, only the exact plane, so memory stays flat however many rows pass through, with Add / Remove / Replace batches applied exactly once by feed position; a per-query usage meter (rows/bytes processed) is available for billing. Integrates as an EvalApp extension: attach it to a pipeline and query it from a step, with async execution.",
